ROADMAP AFTER HANDOVER

1. 🛟 Backup & Data Safety

I agree with our previous ordering: this should be next.

Sprig has crossed an important threshold. It's no longer a toy app containing disposable sample data. You're actually building garden history in it.

And it's still in localStorage.

Before we build more cleverness on top, we should give the gardener a way to get the garden out of the browser and safely back in again.

But I don't think this should just mean a button saying "Download JSON."

We should design a small proper Sprig Backup architecture:

Whole Garden Backup

all persistent Sprig data
one backup package/file
backup creation date
Sprig data/schema version
enough metadata to identify what the backup contains

Restore

select a Sprig backup
validate it before touching current data
recognise incompatible/malformed files
preferably warn what is about to happen
never casually wipe the existing garden

Version/migration groundwork

backups know what version of Sprig's data structure created them
future Sprig can migrate older data instead of saying, "Sorry, 2026 potatoes have become hieroglyphics."

This is data safety, not the pretty PDF exporter. They are separate jobs.

